.TH GLAZE-SESSION 1 "2026-11-10" "Glaze 0.1.0" "Glaze User Commands"
.SH NAME
glaze-session \- launch the Glaze Wayland session environment and supervise its components
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B glaze-session
.I env
.RI [ \-\-backend
.IR auto | sway | glaze | none ]
.br
.B glaze-session
.I check
.RI [ \-\-backend
.IR name ]
.br
.B glaze-session
.I run
.RI [ \-\-backend
.IR name ]
.RB [ \-\-nested ]
.br
.B glaze-session
.I status
.br
.B glaze-session
.BR \-h | \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B glaze-session
prepares and supervises a Glaze Wayland session. It is a developer-mode tool:
it never edits a login manager, a display-manager configuration or any system
file, and the nested run path keeps the component graph inside a window so the
user's existing graphical session is untouched
(see GLAZE.md section 2, "Install safety").
.PP
The command is built from two pieces that are independently unit-tested: a
session plan
.RB ( glaze-session " " env )
that computes the environment variables every Glaze component and application
needs, and a process supervisor
.RB ( glaze-session " " run )
that starts the component graph, detects exits and performs bounded respawns.
.PP
Run
.B glaze-session
with no arguments, or with
.BR \-h ,
to print usage.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.BR env " [\-\-backend " name ]
Print, as POSIX \fBexport\fR lines, the environment a Glaze session must set
before launching applications. This includes the session identity
.RB ( XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP=Glaze ,
.BR XDG_SESSION_DESKTOP=glaze ,
.BR XDG_SESSION_TYPE=wayland ,
.BR GLAZE_SESSION=1 ),
the selected backend in
.BR GLAZE_COMPOSITOR_BACKEND ,
and toolkit hints that make GTK, Qt, Electron, Firefox/SDL applications prefer
Wayland. If
.B XDG_SESSION_ID
is not already set, a deterministic id of the form
.B glaze-<pid>
is generated.
.TP
.BR check " [\-\-backend " name ]
Verify that the runtime pieces a session needs are present. It reports each
check as
.B [ok]
or
.B [MISS]
and exits non-zero if anything is missing. The checks are:
.BR WAYLAND_DISPLAY
must be set, and each default component program for the selected backend must
be found on
.BR PATH .
A missing compositor is still reported even though nested mode can work without
one.
.TP
.BR run " [\-\-backend " name "] [\-\-nested]"
Build the session plan, apply it to the current process, start the default
component graph and supervise it until the last component exits or a
.B SIGINT
or
.B SIGTERM
is received. Exits and respawns are logged to standard error. If no component
was able to start the command refuses to idle and exits non-zero.
.RS
.PP
With
.BR \-\-nested ,
the
.B sway
component is started with an extra
.B \-c /usr/share/glaze/sway-nested.conf
argument so a wlroots compositor runs inside a window on the host session. The
flag is accepted by the other backends and has no effect on them.
.RE
.TP
.B status
Print a JSON snapshot of the environment the session would use: the composed
.B session_id
and the
.B vars
map. This is a development aid; it does not connect to an already running
supervisor.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-backend " name"
Choose the compositor backend to plan for. Accepted values are
.BR auto " (the default), " sway ", " glaze " and " none .
.TP
.B \-\-nested
Run the compositor nested inside the current session (developer mode).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.SH COMPONENT GRAPH
The default components started by
.B run
depend on the backend:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
.B sway
\- a wlroots compositor, started with
.B \-\-unsupported-gpu
and without respawn.
.IP \(bu 2
.B glaze
\- the native
.BR glaze-compositor ,
without respawn.
.IP \(bu 2
.B auto
and
.B none
\- no compositor component.
.RE
.PP
In every case
.B glaze-service
and
.B glaze-shell
are added to the graph so the shell can talk to real application and window
state rather than a fabricated list.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_SESSION_ID
Used as the session id when present; otherwise one is generated.
.TP
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
Checked by the
.B check
subcommand.
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
The directory under which the service control socket is created by the running
session (see
.BR glaze-service (1)).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success. For
.BR run ,
all components stopped cleanly.
.TP
.B 1
A missing component
.RB ( check ),
an unknown subcommand, or a
.B run
where no component started.
.SH NOTES
The GTK4
.BR glaze-shell
binary and the
.BR glaze-service
daemon binary are not present in this repository snapshot; they are being
implemented by other workstreams. Until they exist,
.B glaze-session check
will report them as
.BR [MISS] .
This command's own environment planning and supervision logic is implemented
and unit-tested; runtime session validation requires a Fedora/Wayland host and
is recorded in
.BR PROJECT_STATUS.md .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glaze-compositor (1),
.BR glaze-service (1),
.BR glaze-shell (1),
.BR glaze-settings (1),
.BR glaze (1)
